From f92faa7bbbceb76f8667b33d3442b66540a2e1e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <hibreak@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:47:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] e-ink: outline floating windows instead of dimming behind
 them

With debug.eink.windows=1 the window manager shows no dim layer behind
windows, and dialogs and popup windows draw a 2dp outline along the
outline of their background drawable (black in light mode, white in
dark mode).

An e-ink panel shows the dim layer as dithered grey over the whole
screen, which looks noisy and leaves ghosts when it goes away. On the
Bigme HiBreak Pro the power menu screen was 77% mid-grey. Shadows are
too faint to show a window's edge on such a panel, hence the outline.
It is drawn by DecorView for floating windows and by PopupWindow's
background view, so it covers every app that gives its window a
background drawable. Windows that draw their own surface inside a
transparent window (Compose dialogs) get no outline.

Change-Id: I0c1d2e3f4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293
